{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T10:05:34.218Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02b258e8e56f2fcd016a7af3e0870481908ff4a48918c1f4e0","status":"completed","call_id":"call_YH0E8Q7vXq8k2rWUozGUxkDo","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating/docs/plans/cross-platform-parity-execution.md\\n@@\\n-The renewed focused PTY/TUI suite passes 38 tests with 183 assertions. The full\\n-root suite passes 294 tests with 86,606 assertions, strict root typecheck passes,\\n-and the canonical root build succeeds. T2 remains incomplete: Sessions,\\n-Library, Review, Settings, complete `/shell` context transfer, provider-failure\\n-runtime recovery, unknown-document runtime recovery, and truthful\\n-read/execute/source-mutation capability flows still require the complete\\n-acceptance matrix.\\n+The Sessions browser is now a real project-scoped Pi session surface, available\\n+through Ctrl+S and `/sessions`. It sorts saved sessions by modification time,\\n+marks the active session, exposes message count and parent/fork lineage, and\\n+offers explicit Resume, Resume and rename, whole-branch fork, and earlier-turn\\n+fork actions. The operations use Pi RPC rather than a second Keating session\\n+store. Successful switches clear stale documents, hydrate the selected\\n+transcript and header, and preserve the original session. Earlier-turn forks\\n+restore Pi's exact source prompt into the composer for editing; cancellation\\n+and failures retain the active session.\\n+\\n+An actual 80-column PTY opened the Sessions browser against eight project\\n+sessions. A separate live RPC check switched an ephemeral runtime to the most\\n+recent saved session and confirmed the selected path plus all 152 messages\\n+were hydrated. It did not rename or fork user session files. The deterministic\\n+controller seam verifies the exact rename, clone, fork-message enumeration,\\n+fork dispatch, cancellation, stale-document clearing, and draft restoration\\n+transitions.\\n+\\n+The built-runtime check found that root tsc previously left shared-contract\\n+imports pointing at unpublished TypeScript workspace packages, and that the\\n+Node launcher then entered OpenTUI despite its Bun-only native FFI. Root now\\n+emits the shared contract sources inside `dist`, TUI imports them through\\n+runtime-local bridges, and the root package no longer declares those private\\n+workspaces as install dependencies. `node bin/keating.js tui` hands the exact\\n+invocation to Bun; release bundles are configured to carry a private Bun\\n+binary, while npm installs give an actionable missing-Bun error. A dry-run npm\\n+pack confirms both compiled contract trees and the handoff module are present.\\n+The rebuilt Node entry successfully delegated and opened the real Sessions\\n+browser in ASCII plus semantic `NO_COLOR` mode.\\n+\\n+The renewed focused PTY/TUI/runtime suite passes 47 tests with 222 assertions.\\n+The full root suite passes 300 tests with 86,750 assertions, strict root\\n+typecheck passes, the canonical root build succeeds, and npm pack dry-run\\n+succeeds. T2 remains incomplete: Library, Review, Settings, complete `/shell`\\n+context transfer, live rename/clone/earlier-turn-fork acceptance in an isolated\\n+session directory, provider-failure runtime recovery, unknown-document runtime\\n+recovery, and truthful read/execute/source-mutation capability flows still\\n+require the complete acceptance matrix. The configured release-bundle Bun copy\\n+also remains source/test evidence until an actual release archive is assembled\\n+and launched outside the checkout.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"7237b642-49e1-4cb7-8a12-bea4d7047d25"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T10:05:34.415Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"patch_apply_end","call_id":"exec-0239642d-a5e6-4aed-befd-e79b4b480fa7","turn_id":"7237b642-49e1-4cb7-8a12-bea4d7047d25","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/diogenes/Projects/keating/docs/plans/cross-platform-parity-execution.md\n","stderr":"","success":true,"changes":{"/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/docs/plans/cross-platform-parity-execution.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -942,9 +942,42 @@\n \n-The renewed focused PTY/TUI suite passes 38 tests with 183 assertions. The full\n-root suite passes 294 tests with 86,606 assertions, strict root typecheck passes,\n-and the canonical root build succeeds. T2 remains incomplete: Sessions,\n-Library, Review, Settings, complete `/shell` context transfer, provider-failure\n-runtime recovery, unknown-document runtime recovery, and truthful\n-read/execute/source-mutation capability flows still require the complete\n-acceptance matrix.\n+The Sessions browser is now a real project-scoped Pi session surface, available\n+through Ctrl+S and `/sessions`. It sorts saved sessions by modification time,\n+marks the active session, exposes message count and parent/fork lineage, and\n+offers explicit Resume, Resume and rename, whole-branch fork, and earlier-turn\n+fork actions. The operations use Pi RPC rather than a second Keating session\n+store. Successful switches clear stale documents, hydrate the selected\n+transcript and header, and preserve the original session. Earlier-turn forks\n+restore Pi's exact source prompt into the composer for editing; cancellation\n+and failures retain the active session.\n+\n+An actual 80-column PTY opened the Sessions browser against eight project\n+sessions. A separate live RPC check switched an ephemeral runtime to the most\n+recent saved session and confirmed the selected path plus all 152 messages\n+were hydrated. It did not rename or fork user session files. The deterministic\n+controller seam verifies the exact rename, clone, fork-message enumeration,\n+fork dispatch, cancellation, stale-document clearing, and draft restoration\n+transitions.\n+\n+The built-runtime check found that root tsc previously left shared-contract\n+imports pointing at unpublished TypeScript workspace packages, and that the\n+Node launcher then entered OpenTUI despite its Bun-only native FFI. Root now\n+emits the shared contract sources inside `dist`, TUI imports them through\n+runtime-local bridges, and the root package no longer declares those private\n+workspaces as install dependencies. `node bin/keating.js tui` hands the exact\n+invocation to Bun; release bundles are configured to carry a private Bun\n+binary, while npm installs give an actionable missing-Bun error. A dry-run npm\n+pack confirms both compiled contract trees and the handoff module are present.\n+The rebuilt Node entry successfully delegated and opened the real Sessions\n+browser in ASCII plus semantic `NO_COLOR` mode.\n+\n+The renewed focused PTY/TUI/runtime suite passes 47 tests with 222 assertions.\n+The full root suite passes 300 tests with 86,750 assertions, strict root\n+typecheck passes, the canonical root build succeeds, and npm pack dry-run\n+succeeds. T2 remains incomplete: Library, Review, Settings, complete `/shell`\n+context transfer, live rename/clone/earlier-turn-fork acceptance in an isolated\n+session directory, provider-failure runtime recovery, unknown-document runtime\n+recovery, and truthful read/execute/source-mutation capability flows still\n+require the complete acceptance matrix. The configured release-bundle Bun copy\n+also remains source/test evidence until an actual release archive is assembled\n+and launched outside the checkout.\n \n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed"}}
