{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T10:06:27.266Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"OpenTUI Sessions is now implemented and runtime-verified.\n\n- Ctrl+S and `/sessions` open real project-scoped Pi sessions.\n- Supports resume, rename, whole-branch fork, earlier-turn fork, cancellation, and lineage labels.\n- Live RPC check found eight sessions and hydrated 152 messages after switching.\n- Built `node bin/keating.js tui` now correctly delegates to Bun; standalone releases are configured to bundle Bun.\n- Fixed unpublished workspace-contract imports in the packaged CLI.\n- npm pack includes the compiled shared contracts.\n\nVerification:\n\n- Focused OpenTUI/runtime: 47 tests, 222 assertions\n- Root: 300 tests, 86,750 assertions\n- Typecheck, build, npm pack dry-run: passed\n- Built-entry 80×24 ASCII/`NO_COLOR` PTY: passed\n- `vet`: still blocked by the pre-existing aggregate dirty-diff reconstruction error\n\nEvidence is recorded in [cross-platform-parity-execution.md](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/docs/plans/cross-platform-parity-execution.md:943). The execution graph kept the tightly coupled host/runtime files coordinator-owned and ordered runtime verification after the production build.\n\nT2 still needs Library, Review, Settings, `/shell` context transfer, isolated live fork/rename checks, and capability/code-augmentation flows. No complete weighted node passed, so `/goal` remains active at 13.7%.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
