{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T10:14:17.373Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019ff050-d61d-7e81-b605-a14d88fc6ccc","call_id":"call_VOWy1vl0obqNuh73h9OWxDyX","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"- components had “too much redundant text” and “too many boxes within boxes” -> favor one primary frame, lighter separators, fewer labels/counters, and whitespace-driven grouping; use Storybook/screenshots for diagnosis [Task 1]\n- image streaming should provide a better preview -> show partial visual output and minimize metadata chrome [Task 1]\n- Gemini Live is full audio/video duplex while GPT Realtime is audio duplex with image input -> model/test capability tiers instead of hardcoding provider assumptions [Task 2]\n- when asked to “fix these issues and then deploy the code” -> implement, deterministically validate, deploy, poll to success, and perform public smoke checks [Task 2]\n- Live should be “activatable in chat” like “chatgpt live or gemini live” -> provide one-click in-context entry rather than requiring navigation to `/live`; preserve unrelated dirty-worktree edits during integration [Task 3]\n- study plans should have “at least two layers,” detail, and links between plans -> render explicit navigable stable-plan relationships, not prose-only references [Task 4]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- Storybook runs from `web` on port 6006; regenerate Panda styles with `bun run panda`. OpenAI partial image SSE uses `stream: true`, `partial_images: 2`, and `image_generation.partial_image` events with `b64_json`; retain JSON fallback for non-SSE providers [Task 1]\n- Extract incomplete animation argument strings through `toolcall_delta`; render incomplete HTML sandboxed without scripts. `RunnableCodeBlock` works for `MarkdownBlock` consumers, but the chat `pre` handler still needs wiring for chat code execution [Task 1]\n- Gemini Live accepts sampled JPEG (max one frame/sec), whereas OpenAI Realtime uses static `input_image` items. AudioWorklets require an active output graph; a zero-gain node to destination keeps capture running silently [Task 2]\n- Keating production is Railway `keating` at `https://keating.help`; verify `railway up --detach --service keating` by polling success then public `/`, `/live`, and manifest HTTP checks [Task 2]\n- `AssistantChatPanel.tsx` adds the Live composer action, credential prompting, and `LiveVoiceOverlay`; `live-transcript.ts` accumulates provider-neutral turns, flushes partial turns on shutdown, and `preserveLiveConversation` persists both sides into the active chat. Render full-screen dialog overlays through `createPortal(..., document.body)` with `zIndex: 100`. [Task 3]\n- Camera capture is best-effort: when capture/audio setup fails, keep the interface usable with recovery and dictation fallback. Browser checks covered desktop/mobile entry, missing-key flow, audio-only dialog, camera preview, and 390px geometry; `bun test` (617), typecheck, and build passed. [Task 3]\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"a253b762-0ccd-4d5b-9bfc-adadeef56bed"}}}
