he shared UI contract and design roles.\n   315: | W1 | Web contract adapter | Existing web behavior remains green and the ver...\n   318: | M3 | Mobile learner surfaces | Full local learner journey resumes after for...\n   321: | T1 | Terminal interaction protocol | Every stateful shared OpenUI action su...\n   322: | T2 | OpenTUI learner product | Session, library, review, settings, Markdown...\n   323: | I1 | Cross-surface integration | Consumers use shared contracts/tokens and ...\n   358: T2[\"T2 · OpenTUI product\"]\n  +5\n\n[file] docs/plans/cross-platform-parity-execution.md (91):\n    81: kind             // test | build | package | rendered | device | auth | runtime\n   100: rendered, authenticated, device, or real-provider path.\n   112: | Terminal | T1, T2 | 15% |\n   144: | 3 | M2, T2, D3 | Terra-high implementation; Luna reviews C1/C2 and desktop ...\n   167: | M3 | Terra-high worker | mobile primitives/screens/renderers/tests | server...\n   171: | T2 | Terra-high worker | assigned `src/tui/**`, Pi adapters, TUI tests/tape...\n   201: assert_rendering_matrix_covers_web_markdown_mermaid_and_openui(build)\n   225: web_renderable_markdown_or_mermaid_is_only_shown_as_source,\n   228: model_authored_html_or_javascript_executes_to_render_content\n   363: IF node.requires_rendered_ui:\n   366: evidence += execute_rendering_fixture_pack(\n   393: FUNCTION execute_rendering_fixture_pack(node, families, states, themes):\n   394: fixtures = load_versioned_cross_surface_rendering_fixtures()\n   395: webReference = render_in_packaged_web_or_desktop(fixtures)\n   403: candidate = render_on_required_surface(node.surface, fixtures)\n   416: IF fixture.family == mermaid AND webReference[fixture].rendered:\n   417: assert candidate[fixture].rendered_or_platform_outcome_is_explicit()\n   445: AND rendering_fixture_pack_passes_web_desktop_mobile_and_terminal_outcomes()\n   528: rendered Usage and Learn in light mode, prepared its JSON export in Android's\n   529: share sheet, opened and cancelled the system JSON picker, and rendered the new\n   541: and recovery rendering only, not look parity.\n   543: The subsequent rendering tranche raises current mobile verification to 211\n   548: Assistant output now passes through a bounded GFM AST; common Mermaid\n   549: flowcharts render as native SVG with source fallback. The native subset covers\n   553: model-authored HTML remain inert or consent-gated. Validated shared OpenUI JSON\n  +66\n\n... +71\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"a253b762-0ccd-4d5b-9bfc-adadeef56bed"}}}
