{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T10:16:43.766Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The parity contract is explicit about one important distinction: desktop/mobile must graphically render Mermaid when web can, while OpenTUI must render the full readable source plus description and a preserved-session handoff—it must not pretend terminal graphics exist. The current terminal code already follows that rule; I’m exercising the complete shared Markdown/Mermaid/OpenUI fixture pack now and will close any gaps found in the actual product path.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T10:16:43.766Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_02b258e8e56f2fcd016a7af6898b508190ad904303db041d1e","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The parity contract is explicit about one important distinction: desktop/mobile must graphically render Mermaid when web can, while OpenTUI must render the full readable source plus description and a preserved-session handoff—it must not pretend terminal graphics exist. The current terminal code already follows that rule; I’m exercising the complete shared Markdown/Mermaid/OpenUI fixture pack now and will close any gaps found in the actual product path."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"a253b762-0ccd-4d5b-9bfc-adadeef56bed"}}}
