{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T10:22:15.702Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Implemented and documented this parity tranche.\n\n- OpenTUI now has real Library, Review, and Settings surfaces.\n- Markdown renders through OpenTUI’s semantic Markdown renderer.\n- All declared Mermaid grammars are preserved and tested. Web/desktop/mobile retain graphical rendering requirements; terminal provides readable source and a same-session graphical handoff.\n- Every canonical OpenUI node renders or exposes its approved platform handoff. Stateful actions are durable, retryable, and idempotent.\n- `/shell` now reopens the exact active Pi session, preserving conversation context for code/tool-capable work.\n- Library was validated in a real rebuilt 80×24 PTY.\n\nVerification:\n\n- Full root suite: 307 tests, 86,773 assertions\n- Rendering/OpenUI suite: 34 tests, 217 assertions\n- TypeScript: passed\n- Canonical build: passed\n- `vet`: attempted after every edit, but the final run hit its known `DiffApplicationError` reconstructing the large pre-existing dirty worktree.\n\nEvidence and completion rules are recorded in [cross-platform-parity-execution.md](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/docs/plans/cross-platform-parity-execution.md). The rendering requirements remain defined in [cross-platform-parity-build.md](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/docs/plans/cross-platform-parity-build.md).\n\nThe overall `/goal` remains at 13.7% because this strengthened T2 substantially but did not complete another entire weighted node. Remaining terminal acceptance includes isolated live fork/rename testing, provider-failure recovery, unknown-document runtime recovery, and a visible diff/confirm/validate/rollback code-augmentation flow.\n\n","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":1071,"lineEnd":1079,"note":"Prior Keating rendering and OpenUI context"},{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":1106,"lineEnd":1114,"note":"Prior OpenUI study plan architecture"}],"rolloutIds":["019fbf21-f09f-7430-9d67-c1267e8285ed","019fb1e4-eee4-7662-ba3a-fb1eef03df30"]}}}
