{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T10:26:45.683Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The isolated runtime check exposed a real defect rather than merely missing evidence: cloning immediately after a provider-auth failure throws `Entry … not found`. The original failed prompt is preserved, but Pi’s clone RPC cannot branch from that error-state leaf. I’m tracing that transition now and will make OpenTUI recover visibly without corrupting the original session, then rerun clone/fork on a valid isolated session.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
