{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T10:31:01.895Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02b258e8e56f2fcd016a7af9e46cec8190a55e40bedf06158e","status":"completed","call_id":"call_F4ZLwuEBqagiOSOkkjmVNxgT","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\"cmd\":\"rtk read src/tui/prompt-recovery.ts && rtk proxy sed -n '390,455p' src/tui/host-controller.ts && rtk proxy rg -n \\\"message_end|agent_end\\\" node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/rpc.md node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs -g '*.md' | head -n 80\",\"workdir\":\"/home/diogenes/Projects/keating\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":10000}); text(r.output)\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"336fceb4-26f3-465e-89fc-cad66edcf467"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T10:31:02.097Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019ff060-2ad1-7492-ba30-5a5511eb4a0d","call_id":"call_F4ZLwuEBqagiOSOkkjmVNxgT","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"export interface TuiPromptClient {\n  prompt(message: string): Promise<unknown>;\n  followUp(message: string): Promise<unknown>;\n}\n\nexport type TuiPromptSendOutcome =\n  | { ok: true; message: string }\n  | { ok: false; message: string; error: unknown }\n  | { ok: false; message: null; error: null };\n\n/** Keeps the exact learner draft available until one send is accepted. */\nexport class TuiPromptRecovery {\n  private failedDraft: string | null = null;\n  private failedMessage: string | null = null;\n\n  constructor(private readonly client: TuiPromptClient) {}\n\n  get draft(): string | null {\n    return this.failedDraft;\n  }\n\n  async send(draft: string, busy: boolean, message = draft): Promise<TuiPromptSendOutcome> {\n    try {\n      if (busy) await this.client.followUp(message);\n      else await this.client.prompt(message);\n      this.failedDraft = null;\n      this.failedMessage = null;\n      return { ok: true, message: draft };\n    } catch (error) {\n      this.failedDraft = draft;\n      this.failedMessage = message;\n      return { ok: false, message: draft, error };\n    }\n  }\n\n  async retry(busy: boolean): Promise<TuiPromptSendOutcome> {\n    const message = this.failedDraft;\n    if (message === null) return { ok: false, message: null, error: null };\n    return this.send(message, busy, this.failedMessage ?? message);\n  }\n}\n  handleEvent(event: unknown): void {\n    const candidate = event as { type?: string } | null;\n    if (!candidate || typeof candidate !== \"object\") return;\n\n    switch (candidate.type) {\n      case \"message_update\": {\n        const message = (event as { message?: { role?: string } }).message;\n        if (message?.role === \"assistant\") {\n          const hydrated = transcriptEntriesFromMessages([message]);\n          const entry = hydrated.find((item) => item.kind === \"assistant\");\n          if (entry) this.surface.setStreaming({ ...entry, id: \"assistant-streaming\" });\n        }\n        return;\n      }\n      case \"message_end\": {\n        const message = (event as { message?: { role?: string } }).message;\n        if (message?.role === \"assistant\") {\n          this.surface.setStreaming(null);\n          const entries = transcriptEntriesFromMessages([message]);\n          for (const entry of entries) this.surface.appendEntry({ ...entry, id: this.nextId(entry.kind) });\n        }\n        return;\n      }\n      case \"tool_execution_start\": {\n        const { toolName, args } = event as { toolName?: string; args?: unknown };\n        if (toolName) {\n          const summary = briefArgs(args);\n          this.append(\"tool\", toolName, summary || \"Running…\");\n        }\n        return;\n      }\n      case \"tool_execution_end\": {\n        const { toolName, result, isError } = event as { toolName?: string; result?: unknown; isError?: boolean };\n        if (!toolName) return;\n        if (isError) {\n          this.appendError(`${toolName} failed`, result);\n          return;\n        }\n        if (carriesUiDocument(toolName, result)) {\n          const adapted = adaptToolResultToUiDocument(toolName, result);\n          if (adapted.ok) {\n            this.activateUiDocument(adapted.document);\n            return;\n          }\n          this.append(\"error\", \"Interactive document needs attention\", adapted.recovery.message);\n          return;\n        }\n        const card = toolResultCardLines(toolName, result);\n        if (card) this.append(\"artifact\", `${toolName} result`, card.join(\"\\n\"));\n        else this.append(\"tool\", `${toolName} completed`, messageText(result) || \"Completed\");\n        return;\n      }\n      case \"agent_start\":\n        this.surface.setHeaderState({ busy: true });\n        return;\n      case \"agent_end\":\n        this.surface.setHeaderState({ busy: false });\n        return;\n      case \"extension_ui_request\":\n        this.handleUiRequest(event as UiRequestEvent);\n        return;\n      case \"ui_document\": {\n        const { document } = event as { document?: unknown };\n        this.activateUiDocument(document);\n        return;\n      }\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/rpc.md:753:| `agent_end` | Agent completes (includes all generated messages) |\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/rpc.md:758:| `message_end` | Message completes |\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/rpc.md:777:### agent_end\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/rpc.md:783:  \"type\": \"agent_end\",\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/rpc.md:804:### message_start / message_end\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/rpc.md:810:{\"type\": \"message_end\", \"message\": {...}}\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/rpc.md:1351:    if event.get(\"type\") == \"agent_end\":\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/rpc.md:753:| `agent_end` | Agent completes (includes all generated messages) |\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/rpc.md:758:| `message_end` | Message completes |\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/rpc.md:777:### agent_end\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/rpc.md:783:  \"type\": \"agent_end\",\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/rpc.md:804:### message_start / message_end\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/rpc.md:810:{\"type\": \"message_end\", \"message\": {...}}\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/rpc.md:1351:    if event.get(\"type\") == \"agent_end\":\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/json.md:31:  | { type: \"agent_end\"; messages: AgentMessage[] }\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/json.md:38:  | { type: \"message_end\"; message: AgentMessage }\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/json.md:73:{\"type\":\"message_end\",\"message\":{...}}\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/json.md:75:{\"type\":\"agent_end\",\"messages\":[...]}\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/json.md:81:pi --mode json \"List files\" 2>/dev/null | jq -c 'select(.type == \"message_end\")'\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/extensions.md:291:  ├─► message_start / message_update / message_end         │\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/extensions.md:309:  └─► agent_end                                            │\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/extensions.md:534:#### agent_start / agent_end\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/extensions.md:541:pi.on(\"agent_end\", async (event, ctx) => {\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/extensions.md:560:#### message_start / message_update / message_end\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/extensions.md:564:- `message_start` and `message_end` fire for user, assistant, and toolResult messages.\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/extensions.md:566:- `message_end` handlers can return `{ message }` to replace the finalized message. The replacement must keep the same `role`.\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/extensions.md:578:pi.on(\"message_end\", async (event, ctx) => {\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/extensions.md:2639:| `git-merge-and-resolve.ts` | Fetch, merge, and resolve conflicts | `on(\"agent_end\")`, `exec`, `sendUserMessage` |\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/custom-provider.md:545:If your provider returns overflow errors with a message pi does not recognize, normalize the error from the same extension that registers the provider. Use a `message_end` handler to rewrite the assistant message so its `errorMessage` starts with a phrase pi recognizes. The generic fallback `context_length_exceeded` is the safest choice.\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/custom-provider.md:553:  pi.on(\"message_end\", (event, ctx) => {\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/custom-provider.md:577:`message_end` runs before pi tracks the assistant message for auto-compaction, so the rewritten `errorMessage` is what pi checks. With this in place, pi will:\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/sdk.md:298:    case \"message_end\":\nnode_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs/sdk.md:306:    case \"agent_end\":\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"336fceb4-26f3-465e-89fc-cad66edcf467"}}}
