{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T10:42:02.315Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02b258e8e56f2fcd016a7afc7758908190ad33adca75449cb9","status":"completed","call_id":"call_E7ftyE2ZkrftmPWrfQw1yihK","name":"exec","input":"const results = await Promise.all([\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk read /home/diogenes/.codex/skills/plan-execution-graph/references/template.md\",workdir:\"/home/diogenes/Projects/keating\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:8000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk proxy sed -n '492,535p' /home/diogenes/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\",workdir:\"/home/diogenes/Projects/keating\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:6000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rtk git status --short -- desktop web/src/keating/oauth.ts web/src/components/settings/CloudProviderKeysSection.tsx docs/plans/cross-platform-parity-build.md docs/plans/cross-platform-parity-execution.md docs/plans/cross-platform-parity-baseline.md\",workdir:\"/home/diogenes/Projects/keating\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:5000})\n]); results.forEach((r,i)=>text(`---${i}---\\n${r.output}`));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"93ef4b9d-3191-46b6-a2c2-3b39e130995b"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T10:42:02.564Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019ff06a-3ec4-7531-82c6-5585501205bd","call_id":"call_E7ftyE2ZkrftmPWrfQw1yihK","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---0---\n# Execution Graph Template\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    P0[\"P0 · Coordinator preflight\"]\n    A[\"A · Explorer or foundation\"]\n    B[\"B · Shared contract\"]\n    C[\"C · Feature slice\"]\n    I[\"I · Coordinator integration\"]\n    T[\"T · Tests and builds\"]\n    R[\"R · Runtime verification\"]\n\n    P0 --> A\n    P0 --> B\n    A --> C\n    B --> C\n    C --> I\n    I --> T\n    T --> R\n```\n\n## Waves\n\n| Wave | Ready nodes | Gate |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | P0 | Baseline and ownership recorded |\n| 1 | A, B | Foundations complete |\n| 2 | C and independent feature nodes | Focused checks pass |\n| 3 | I | Integrated tree is coherent |\n| 4 | T, then R | Static and runtime verification pass |\n\n## Agent Contract\n\n### Node ID - Name\n\n- **Role:** worker, explorer, verifier, or coordinator\n- **Depends on:** node IDs\n- **Owns:** exact files or subsystem\n- **Produces:** concrete artifact or answer\n- **Must not edit:** conflicting or protected files\n- **Acceptance:** objective completion checks\n\n## Coordinator Gate\n\n- Review patches and ownership.\n- Resolve shared-file integration.\n- Refresh generated artifacts.\n- Run repository-native verification.\n- Validate the real runtime path.\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---1---\n# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating production subscription OAuth and Railway verification\nscope: Reload-safe subscription OAuth for OpenAI Codex, Anthropic, and GitHub Copilot, production deployment, and truthful end-to-end acceptance checks.\napplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reuse OAuth paths and verification gates for the same providers; provider authorization/account state and live credential consumption must be re-exercised.\n\n## Task 1: Restore production subscription OAuth end to end\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/03/rollout-2026-08-03T19-02-36-019fc9dd-5f25-7822-81e2-7d554d1a2685.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-04T01:08:37+00:00, thread_id=019fc9dd-5f25-7822-81e2-7d554d1a2685, partial; deployed and route-checked, live OpenAI exchange/model use unverified)\n\n### keywords\n\n- oauth.ts, CloudProviderKeysSection.tsx, keating_oauth_pending, PKCE, getPendingOAuthRequest, cancelPendingOAuthRequest, /api/oauth/token, /api/oauth/refresh, OpenAI Codex, Anthropic, GitHub Copilot, Railway\n\n## Task 2: Add native Anthropic and OpenAI Codex subscription provider support\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/08/10/rollout-2026-08-10T01-22-18-019fea1f-2888-7840-b378-17490c07c932.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-10T05:31:15+00:00, thread_id=019fea1f-2888-7840-b378-17490c07c932, success; live authorization/model request unverified)\n\n### keywords\n\n- openai-codex, openai-codex-responses, pi-ai, ChatGPT OAuth JWT, chatgpt-account-id, Anthropic OAuth, PKCE, oauth-provider-config.ts, nodepod-boot-files.ts\n\n## User preferences\n\n- OAuth should be “working in prod” and “testable end to end” -> verify provider authorization, callback completion, persistence, refresh, credential consumption, deployment, and one authenticated model request; unit tests/callback rendering alone are insufficient [Task 1]\n- preserve unrelated dirty-worktree edits when modifying the checkout [Task 1]\n- when the user asked to “use the anthropic and codex sdk and for sign in and support for those models in keating” -> use native provider semantics rather than ordinary API-key fallback [Task 2]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- Main files are `web/src/keating/oauth.ts`, `web/src/components/settings/CloudProviderKeysSection.tsx`, `web/src/test/oauth.test.ts`, and generated `web/src/keating/nodepod-boot-files.ts`. Store pending safe metadata under `keating_oauth_pending`; recover with `getPendingOAuthRequest()` and cancel with `cancelPendingOAuthRequest()` without exposing PKCE verifier/state. [Task 1]\n- Pending safe metadata stays under `keating_oauth_pending`; `getPendingOAuthRequest()` must not expose PKCE verifier/state. UI tells users the expected localhost error page can be copied back into “Finish sign-in below.” [Task 1][Task 2]\n- Codex remains a distinct `openai-codex` provider: `providerToOAuthId(\"openai\")` is intentionally null, while `openai-codex` maps to `openai-codex`. pi-ai's `openai-codex-responses` transport consumes the ChatGPT OAuth JWT directly, derives account ID, and sends Bearer plus `chatgpt-account-id`; exchanging it for a normal OpenAI API key breaks the subscription route. Anthropic OAuth passes through to the Anthropic transport, which supplies OAuth headers; do not convert it to `x-api-key`. [Task 2]\n- OAuth token/refresh now return upstream data without the obsolete Codex `id_token` -> OpenAI API-key exchange; `web/server/api/oauth/openai-codex.ts` was removed. Regenerate `web/src/keating/nodepod-boot-files.ts` with `bun scripts/generate-nodepod-boot-files.ts` after OAuth source changes. [Task 2]\n- 604 web tests, typecheck, and web build passed. Railway deployment `fca2021d-0965-4761-a5ee-5470da179944` succeeded; `https://keating.help/`, `/chat`, error callback, malformed token (400), and GitHub device endpoint (safe 200 response) were checked. [Task 1]\n- The native integration passed focused OAuth/provider tests (24), full web tests (796 across 123 files), typecheck, and production build; subscription UI cards are labeled “Subscription sign-in,” with unauthenticated models routing to Models & Providers. [Task 2]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- OpenAI reached `Phone number required`; never enter personal data. Live exchange and an authenticated model request remain unverified until the user completes provider verification. Playwriter timeouts/disconnects and the unrelated `useSeo.ts` null-remove error are browser/runtime harness issues, not OAuth route proof. [Task 1]\n- Vet encountered an untracked-file bug then lacked Anthropic credentials; do not claim it passed. [Task 1]\n- A focused fixture can fail when expiry falls inside the 60-second refresh window; use a test credential with more than 60 seconds remaining. Vet's `DiffApplicationError` against a dirty worktree is unverified review, not a code finding. Live OAuth authorization and model use still require provider accounts. [Task 2]\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---2---\n M desktop/package.json\n M desktop/src/ipc.ts\n M desktop/src/main.ts\n D desktop/src/preload.ts\n M desktop/tsconfig.json\n M web/src/components/settings/CloudProviderKeysSection.tsx\n M web/src/keating/oauth.ts\n?? desktop/release/\n?? desktop/scripts/\n?? desktop/src/lifecycle.ts\n?? desktop/src/nitro-runtime.ts\n?? desktop/src/permissions.ts\n?? desktop/src/preload.cts\n?? desktop/src/runtime-paths.ts\n?? desktop/src/security.ts\n?? desktop/test/\n?? docs/plans/cross-platform-parity-baseline.md\n?? docs/plans/cross-platform-parity-build.md\n?? docs/plans/cross-platform-parity-execution.md"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"93ef4b9d-3191-46b6-a2c2-3b39e130995b"}}}
