{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T10:42:07.044Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_02b258e8e56f2fcd016a7afc7ecf788190a71a7982f173d3c9","name":"list_agents","namespace":"collaboration","arguments":"{}","call_id":"call_FMeRYembwop5AjLXaFb3dKcz","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"93ef4b9d-3191-46b6-a2c2-3b39e130995b"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T10:42:07.128Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_019ff06a-5098-7e93-bacc-3ddbc0604894","call_id":"call_FMeRYembwop5AjLXaFb3dKcz","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/d2_gap_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"D2 is unaccepted. The current execution document correctly treats its 12 desktop tests and headless package startup as insufficient: no installed-window, API, WebSocket, permission, restart, or clean-profile evidence exists.\\n\\n| D2 concern | Current evidence | Audit result |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Navigation/external links | Main process restricts renderer navigation to the local Nitro origin and externalizes safe HTTPS/mailto links. Pure policy tests cover URL predicates. | Source-level implementation only; no installed-window exercise. |\\n| IPC limits | Sandboxed, context-isolated preload exposes only P2P RPC; main validates origin, sender WebContents, method, payload size/depth, and replayed IDs. | Good source foundation, but no actual Electron IPC/foreign-renderer runtime test. |\\n| Permissions | No `setPermissionCheckHandler`, `setPermissionRequestHandler`, or display-media policy appears in desktop source. | Missing implementation. This contradicts the required “Electron permission-controlled web Live” outcome. |\\n| OAuth recovery | Web OAuth begins with `window.open(\\\"about:blank\\\")`; desktop’s `setWindowOpenHandler` denies all non-safe external URLs, and `about:blank` is neither HTTPS nor mailto. | Concrete functional blocker: OAuth cannot open its initial popup in Electron. There is also no desktop deep-link handling. |\\n| OS secret storage | OAuth credentials go through `ProviderKeysStore`; in desktop that backend is P2P IPC. No Electron `safeStorage`/keychain adapter exists. | Missing required main-owned OS secret storage boundary. |\\n| Local Courses | Packaged Nitro creates user-data course/Pear directories and uses `/api/courses/session` for readiness. | Plausible source/package wiring only; no local course list/workspace/cookie/WebSocket exercised in a desktop window. |\\n| Sharing state | Share cache/settings use renderer `localStorage`; public share uses same-origin `/api/share`. | Web implementation is inherited, but no desktop persistence/share flow is exercised; it is not P2P-backed. |\\n| Persistence | P2P store is placed under Electron `userData`; web storage swaps to the P2P backend when preload exists. | Source plus headless startup only; no fresh-profile write → quit → reopen proof for sessions/artifacts/settings. |\\n| Package/runtime | `linux-unpacked` includes staged Nitro and the binary survived a 12-second headless launch. | Package/startup evidence, not an installed artifact or visible product verification. |\\n\\nThe OAuth issue is the most immediate code defect: [oauth.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/web/src/keating/oauth.ts:191) opens `about:blank`, while [main.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/desktop/src/main.ts:89) unconditionally denies it. The exact D2 requirement and architecture require exercised OAuth recovery, permission control, persistence, etc., not merely shared web source.\\n\\nRecommended smallest dependency-ready local tranche, without hosted credentials:\\n\\n1. Add an Electron-owned permission policy module for microphone, camera, and display capture, allowlisted to the current loopback Nitro origin; test allow/deny/untrusted-origin paths with mocked Electron session hooks.\\n2. Add a narrow validated `openExternal` preload API (or equivalent desktop-aware OAuth launcher) and change OAuth initiation to use it in Electron. Preserve the existing manual callback-paste recovery, so no real provider account is needed to test the failure/pending/recovery UI.\\n3. Add a main-owned encrypted secret adapter using Electron OS storage for provider/OAuth credentials; test with opaque dummy credentials and migration/recovery paths.\\n4. Add a desktop runtime acceptance harness that launches `linux-unpacked` outside the checkout with a fresh user-data directory, verifies `/chat`, a real `/api/courses/session` local cookie response, session/artifact write–restart–restore, local sharing state, safe external navigation, and denied media permission recovery. It should capture 1024px and 1440px installed windows.\\n5. Only then run the remaining credential-independent Courses workspace and Live permission scenarios. Real OAuth authorization and hosted provider inference remain separate evidence, not simulated success.\\n\\nNo files were changed and I did not rerun test/build commands during this read-only audit.\\n\\n\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/mobile_aggregate_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Parity is not yet runtime-accepted.\\n\\n- Shared trusted OpenUI compiler: solid; malformed, partial, unsafe, and future inputs fail closed.\\n- Web: GFM, math, Mermaid, and OpenUI work, but actual chat uses a reduced renderer versus `/rendering-smoke`; spoilers, highlighting, runnable code, and streaming-fence behavior are missing.\\n- Mobile: all Mermaid grammars and OpenUI ingress are implemented, but mixed-format inline math bypasses KaTeX and code lacks highlighting. Tests do not mount the Expo DOM renderer.\\n- Desktop: inherits the web build, but desktop tests cover only lifecycle/security—not rendered Markdown/Mermaid/OpenUI or reload.\\n- TUI: canonical-document unit tests pass, but no production code emits the `ui_document` event consumed by the host. The live controls are therefore unreachable. Markdown remains raw terminal text; Mermaid is source plus handoff.\\n- Device verification is blocked currently: `adb devices -l` returned no devices.\\n\\nFocused verification passed:\\n\\n- Shared: 12 tests\\n- Web: 46 tests\\n- Mobile: 315 tests\\n- TUI: 25 tests\\n- Desktop: 12 tests plus typecheck\\n\\nThe complete evidence and recommended commands were sent to the coordinator.\\n\\n\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/t2_gap_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Read-only T2 audit: the terminal has a credible T1 foundation, but T2 remains a single-session transcript host, not the required OpenTUI learner product. The execution record agrees: its complete T2 matrix is explicitly open. [execution plan](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/docs/plans/cross-platform-parity-execution.md:911)\\n\\nWhat is working:\\n\\n- Pi RPC, production tool-result adaptation, canonical OpenUI document activation, keyboard-dispatched actions, receiver ACKs, and owner-only idempotent action journals are real foundations. [opentui-host.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/opentui-host.ts:38), [host-controller.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/host-controller.ts:398), [rpc-action-transport.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/ui/rpc-action-transport.ts:101)\\n- Canonical questions, grouped questions, quizzes, goals, study plans, notes, deck ratings, artifact saves, and explicit handoff nodes have keyboard controls. [host-controller.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/host-controller.ts:482)\\n- Mermaid is truthfully non-graphical and includes readable source. Media includes provenance/URI text. [render.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/ui/render.ts:51)\\n- The documented real PTY run proves tool-command discovery and one durable action, but not the T2 product matrix. [execution plan](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/docs/plans/cross-platform-parity-execution.md:918)\\n\\nConcrete T2 gaps:\\n\\n| Gate area | Current state / missing behavior | Authoritative evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Sessions | Hydrates only the active session and can start a new one. No session list, resume, rename, fork UI, branch lineage, export/import/share, or session navigation. The underlying RPC client already exposes switch, rename, fork, and fork-message methods. | [host-controller.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/host-controller.ts:156), [pty-rpc-client.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/runtime/pty-rpc-client.ts:197) |\\n| Library | No Library route, artifact index, open/copy/delete/export actions, or retained unknown-document shelf. Artifacts are only appended into the transcript. | [opentui-host.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/opentui-host.ts:292), [view-model.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/view-model.ts:34) |\\n| Review | A deck sent in the active document can be rated, but there is no due-card queue, Coming Up/review view, learner profile, or review resume flow. | [host-controller.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/host-controller.ts:535) |\\n| Settings | Only cyclic model and thinking controls exist. No settings destination or truthful provider/capability, privacy, diagnostics, data, or retry controls. | [view-model.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/view-model.ts:27) |\\n| Markdown | Assistant messages and OpenUI Markdown are printed as raw text/split lines. There is no terminal Markdown rendering for headings, tables, lists, links, code, spoilers, math fallback, streaming fences, or code handoff. This fails the “no raw syntax replacing a construct” requirement. | [view-model.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/view-model.ts:139), [render.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/ui/render.ts:37), [build spec](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/docs/plans/cross-platform-parity-build.md:198) |\\n| OpenUI ingress/recovery | Canonical JSON and legacy `keating.ui` work. Browser source programs are rejected but not preserved as a retained source/handoff document; unknown future canonical nodes reject the complete document rather than remaining saved/recoverable. | [adapter.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/ui/adapter.ts:151), [build spec](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/docs/plans/cross-platform-parity-build.md:202) |\\n| Mermaid/media handoff | Source/provenance is shown, but concept-map “handoff” only appends text; it neither creates a durable handoff action nor carries a capable-surface target/session context. Image/media nodes can save, but do not expose an equivalent context-preserving open handoff. | [host-controller.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/host-controller.ts:552), [render.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/ui/render.ts:54) |\\n| Provider failure recovery | A failed prompt clears the composer before the RPC call; catch only appends an error. There is no draft restoration or retry-last-prompt action, so learner input can be lost. | [opentui-host.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/opentui-host.ts:372) |\\n| Narrow/wide | The only responsive rule hides the activity rail below 100 columns. No 80×24/100×30/140×40 layout tests or height-aware degradation exist. | [view-model.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/view-model.ts:175) |\\n| Color/no-color | The host hard-codes amber/cream hex colors and Unicode glyphs. It does not consume the existing design-contract terminal profile, detect truecolor/256/16/`NO_COLOR`, or offer ASCII fallback. | [opentui-host.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/opentui-host.ts:54), [view-model.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/view-model.ts:130), [contract.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/packages/design-contract/src/contract.ts:373) |\\n| `/shell` | The command exits correctly, but launches classic Pi with empty args and passes neither current session path nor draft/context. No runtime test covers the switch. | [opentui-host.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/tui/opentui-host.ts:318), [main.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/src/cli/main.ts:506) |\\n| Capability/code augmentation truth | No surface shows available read/execute/patch tools, proposed diff, confirmation, validation, rollback, or an explicit unavailable state. The final T2 scenario requires this. | [execution plan](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/docs/plans/cross-platform-parity-execution.md:999) |\\n\\nTest-evidence gap:\\n\\n- Existing tests are largely controller/journal/mock-RPC tests; no test invokes `launchOpenTui`, drives rendered keyboard navigation, or verifies `/shell`. [opentui-host.test.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/test/opentui-host.test.ts:1), [tui-rpc-action-transport.test.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/test/tui-rpc-action-transport.test.ts:1)\\n- The optional real-model E2E directly uses the RPC client, not the OpenTUI renderer or terminal-size/color matrix. [tui.e2e.test.ts](/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/test/e2e/tui.e2e.test.ts:16)\\n\\nSmallest dependency-ready implementation tranche, requiring neither devices nor hosted credentials:\\n\\n1. Add a terminal presentation profile adapter that consumes `@keating/design-contract`, detects/injects truecolor/256/16/none plus Unicode/ASCII, and eliminates hard-coded host colors/glyphs.\\n2. Add a pure terminal Markdown renderer exercised against the shared fixture pack: readable heading/list/table/link/code/math/source states, bounded horizontal scrolling or wrapping, and safe explicit targets.\\n3. Make composer failure recovery durable in-memory: restore exact draft after send failure and add Retry last prompt; preserve source-program/unknown-document input as a saved recovery/handoff artifact.\\n4. Add deterministic layout tests at 80×24, 100×30, 140×40 across all profile modes, plus no-color/ASCII snapshots.\\n\\nThis is independent of credentials and physical devices, directly addresses the current T2 visual/rendering/recovery blockers, and establishes primitives needed for the next tranche: Sessions (using existing `switchSession`, `setSessionName`, `fork`), Library, Review, Settings, and a context-preserving `/shell` transition. It does not itself make T2 acceptable; the required real-terminal matrix still follows.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"93ef4b9d-3191-46b6-a2c2-3b39e130995b"}}}
