{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T10:43:35.734Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_019ff06b-aab6-79f2-944f-5b57ac86c4ba","author":"/root/d2_current_audit","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/d2_current_audit\nPayload:\nD2 audit result: the first priority code gap is OS-backed OAuth credential storage. Desktop currently routes credentials into generic provider-key storage, not an Electron-owned secret vault. The smallest viable fix is a validated `safeStorage` credential bridge in main/preload, used only by OAuth save/load/delete, with focused vault and OAuth bridge tests.\n\nNext: desktop lacks an actual OAuth callback/deep-link receiver; Codex’s loopback callback is configured but no listener is present. Screen capture is intentionally denied pending a learner-visible picker.\n\nRuntime-only gates still needed: real mic/camera, chosen screen source, OAuth return, course WebSocket, clean outside-checkout install, and 1024/1440 visual comparison. I made no changes or ran tests.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"93ef4b9d-3191-46b6-a2c2-3b39e130995b"}}}
