{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T10:53:44.668Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The secure-storage integration is now complete at source level:\n\n- all desktop `provider-keys` operations route through the Electron credential bridge;\n- new and OAuth credentials never enter replicated P2P storage;\n- legacy P2P credentials migrate only after encrypted persistence succeeds;\n- missing OS encryption fails closed with a recoverable error;\n- direct generic P2P attempts against `provider-keys` are rejected.\n\nThe focused desktop vault/service gate passes 26 tests with 159 assertions, the web routing gate passes 4 tests, and both desktop and web strict typechecks pass. I’m moving into the canonical suites and packaged runtime now.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
