{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T10:57:00.625Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The packaged runtime exposes both preload bridges, rejects generic P2P credential bypass, and—on this Linux host—truthfully reports that secure OS encryption is unavailable. No dummy secret was written anywhere. That surfaced one UI recovery gap: the direct API-key field’s blur handler did not catch storage failures, so the runtime error could become console-only. I’m fixing that now so the entered key remains visible and the exact secure-storage error appears beside the field.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T10:57:00.625Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_02b258e8e56f2fcd016a7afffaa18481909d33ee6cf34c8d3f","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The packaged runtime exposes both preload bridges, rejects generic P2P credential bypass, and—on this Linux host—truthfully reports that secure OS encryption is unavailable. No dummy secret was written anywhere. That surfaced one UI recovery gap: the direct API-key field’s blur handler did not catch storage failures, so the runtime error could become console-only. I’m fixing that now so the entered key remains visible and the exact secure-storage error appears beside the field."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"93ef4b9d-3191-46b6-a2c2-3b39e130995b"}}}
