{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T11:05:00.009Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_019ff07f-4369-76e0-ab67-37fefe02bd2c","call_id":"call_Liw9CNO8100DLz3xRKF3Llq4","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/d2_current_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"D2 audit result: the first priority code gap is OS-backed OAuth credential storage. Desktop currently routes credentials into generic provider-key storage, not an Electron-owned secret vault. The smallest viable fix is a validated `safeStorage` credential bridge in main/preload, used only by OAuth save/load/delete, with focused vault and OAuth bridge tests.\\n\\nNext: desktop lacks an actual OAuth callback/deep-link receiver; Codex’s loopback callback is configured but no listener is present. Screen capture is intentionally denied pending a learner-visible picker.\\n\\nRuntime-only gates still needed: real mic/camera, chosen screen source, OAuth return, course WebSocket, clean outside-checkout install, and 1024/1440 visual comparison. I made no changes or ran tests.\\n\\n\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/desktop_credential_vault\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Implemented the D2 credential-vault foundation.\\n\\n- New: `desktop/src/credential-vault.ts`\\n- New: `desktop/test/credential-vault.test.ts`\\n\\nChecks passed:\\n\\n- Focused vault tests: 7 passing, 79 assertions\\n- `desktop` TypeScript check passed\\n- Scoped `git diff --check` passed\\n- `vet` was invoked immediately but remains blocked by the existing repository-wide dirty-tree `DiffApplicationError`.\\n\\nIntegration contract: construct `CredentialVault({ path, codec })`, where `codec` implements Electron-compatible `isEncryptionAvailable()`, `encryptString()`, and `decryptString()`. The module is Electron-import-free and exposes async `get/set/delete/keys/has/clear`.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/desktop_oauth_callback\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"}]}","intern